{"name":"Beetroot","hex":"#663f44","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beetroot","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A normally deep-red-colored root vegetable usually cooked or pickled before eating.","The edible part of the root of a beet plant, raw or prepared."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To turn a bright red or purple color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beetroot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beetroot","blocks":[{"text":"Beetroot or beet is the taproot portion of a Beta vulgaris subsp. vulgaris plant in the Conditiva Group. The plant is a root vegetable also known as the table beet, garden beet, or dinner beet, or else categorized by color as red beet or golden beet. Its leaves constitute a leaf vegetable called beet greens. It is native to the Azores, Western Europe to the Mediterranean and India.\nBeetroot can be eaten raw, roasted, steamed, or boiled. Beetroot can also be canned, either whole or cut up, and often are pickled, spiced, or served in a sweet-and-sour sauce."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Detroitdarkredbeets.png/330px-Detroitdarkredbeets.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beetroot","wikidata":"Q165437"},{"title":"Beetroot (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Beetroot is the fourth album by the English band Cast, released on 30 July 2001. From the album, a single was released, \"Desert Drought\", which reached #45 in the UK Singles Chart. Two further intended singles, \"Kingdoms And Crowns\" and \"Giving It All Away\" were cancelled due to the album and first single's poor sales."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bc/Beetrootcastcover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beetroot_(album)","wikidata":"Q4880219"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Beets-